      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T10:07:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "resolveSubmodule picks the copy while dependencies are still being listed and hands it over through resolvedSubmodules, so readDependencyModels has to consult that map first, and when nothing fits the same submodule is read from the store a second time in tryToReadModel. Could the include instead carry the parent\u0027s semver and have the read step apply the submodule rule on the one list it reads?",
      "revId": "864c462e0f538a3a4631f7fff8860ef972c0adab",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "00b2d5b1_5257f94d",
        "filename": "modules/gnmi-sb/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/gnmi/southbound/schema/impl/SchemaContextHolderImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 29
      },
      "lineNbr": 545,
      "author": {
        "id": 8324
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T10:07:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The loader stores a model with an openconfig-version under that semver, not its revision, so an import like openconfig-interfaces with revision-date 2021-04-06 never hits this key and is reported missing, although the exact file is stored (it worked before via the single-copy fallback). Could we fall back to reading all copies and matching the newest revision statement in the body?",
      "revId": "864c462e0f538a3a4631f7fff8860ef972c0adab",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
